Bilkul. Aapka setup Google Sheet → Apps Script → Evolution API → WhatsApp hoga, aur Evolution API ko Oracle Cloud Always Free VM + Docker par permanently run karenge.

Aapke case mein ye architecture best rahega:

Google Sheet
    ↓
Google Apps Script
    ↓ HTTPS
Oracle Cloud Public IP / Domain
    ↓
Nginx / Cloudflare Tunnel
    ↓
Evolution API Docker
    ↓
WhatsApp

Aapka Evolution API abhi local Windows machine par localhost:3000 par chal raha hai aur WhatsApp sending bhi test ho chuki hai. Ab usko Oracle Cloud par shift kar denge.

Oracle ke current Always Free resources mein Ampere A1 ke total 2 OCPU + 12 GB RAM available hain, isliye 2 OCPU + 8 GB RAM ka VM comfortably banaya ja sakta hai.

Step 1 — Oracle Cloud VM banana

Oracle Cloud Console mein:

Compute → Instances → Create Instance

Settings:

Name
evolution-api
Image
Ubuntu 24.04

Oracle currently Ubuntu 24.04 ke ARM/AArch64 images provide karta hai, jo Ampere A1 ke liye suitable hain.

Shape

Select:

VM.Standard.A1.Flex

Resources:

OCPU: 2
Memory: 8 GB

Oracle ke Always Free allowance mein 2 OCPU aur 12 GB memory total available hai, so 2 OCPU + 8 GB ek safe configuration hai.

Networking

Ensure:

Assign a public IPv4 address

Oracle ke official guidance mein public IP assign karna bhi recommended deployment flow ka part hai.

SSH Key

Generate SSH key pair select karke private key download kar lena.

Example:

evolution-api.key

Is file ko safe rakhna.

Step 2 — Oracle VM mein SSH

Windows PowerShell se:

ssh -i "C:\Users\YOUR_NAME\Downloads\evolution-api.key" ubuntu@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP

Example:

ssh -i "C:\Users\Akash\Downloads\evolution-api.key" ubuntu@152.xxx.xxx.xxx

Login hone ke baad:

sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
Step 3 — Docker install

Ubuntu par:

sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose-v2

Check:

docker --version

and:

docker compose version

Docker ko startup par enable:

sudo systemctl enable docker
sudo systemctl start docker

Check:

sudo systemctl status docker
Step 4 — Evolution API folder
mkdir -p ~/evolution-api
cd ~/evolution-api

Ab hum yahan:

docker-compose.yml
.env

rakhenge.

Evolution API v2 officially Docker installation support karta hai.

Step 5 — Evolution API Docker setup

Yahan ek important point hai:

Aap Evolution API v2.3.7 use kar rahe ho, isliye hum aapke currently working version ko hi Oracle par replicate karenge, instead of blindly latest version use karne ke.

docker-compose.yml mein roughly:

services:


  evolution-api:
    container_name: evolution_api
    image: atendai/evolution-api:v2.3.7
    restart: always


    ports:
      - "3000:8080"


    env_file:
      - .env


    volumes:
      - evolution_instances:/evolution/instances


volumes:
  evolution_instances:

Lekin isko abhi run mat karna.

Pehle .env properly banayenge.

Step 6 — .env

Example:

SERVER_TYPE=http
SERVER_PORT=8080


AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=YOUR_LONG_RANDOM_API_KEY


DATABASE_ENABLED=false


CACHE_REDIS_ENABLED=false


LOG_LEVEL=ERROR

Aapka existing API key agar:

AkashEvolution2026@123456

hai to production mein main recommend karunga ki Oracle par new long random key use karein.

For example:

AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=EVOL_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
Step 7 — Evolution API start
cd ~/evolution-api

Then:

docker compose up -d

Check:

docker ps

Aapko kuch aisa dikhna chahiye:

evolution_api    Up

Logs:

docker logs -f evolution_api

Agar API properly start ho gayi:

Evolution API

related startup messages dikhenge.

Step 8 — Oracle firewall

Ye bahut important hai.

Oracle Cloud mein sirf Ubuntu firewall open karna enough nahi hota. VCN Security List / Network Security Group mein bhi required port allow karna padta hai.

Temporary testing ke liye:

TCP
Port: 3000
Source: 0.0.0.0/0

But production mein directly 3000 public expose nahi karna better hai.

Final architecture main ye rakhunga:

Internet
   ↓
HTTPS 443
   ↓
Cloudflare
   ↓
Evolution API

Port 3000 ko public nahi rakhna padega.

Step 9 — Test Evolution API

Oracle VM ke andar:

curl http://localhost:3000

Agar response Evolution API ka aa gaya, Docker/API working hai.

Phir browser se:

http://YOUR_ORACLE_PUBLIC_IP:3000

test kar sakte hain.

Expected response approximately Evolution API ka welcome/status response hoga.

Step 10 — WhatsApp instance create karna

Ab Evolution API ke through:

Calco-Bot

instance banayenge.

Aapka existing instance name bhi:

Calco-Bot

hai, jo aapke previous testing mein use hua tha.

Instance create hone ke baad QR code milega.

WhatsApp phone mein:

WhatsApp
→ Linked devices
→ Link a device
→ QR scan

QR scan kar dena.

Step 11 — Pehle Oracle se direct WhatsApp test

Google Sheet ko abhi touch nahi karna.

Pehle Oracle Evolution API se WhatsApp send test karenge.

Example:

curl -X POST "http://localhost:3000/message/sendText/Calco-Bot" \
-H "apikey: YOUR_API_KEY" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{
  "number": "919XXXXXXXXX",
  "text": "Test message from Oracle Evolution API"
}'

Agar WhatsApp par message aa gaya:

Oracle Cloud
     ↓
Docker
     ↓
Evolution API
     ↓
WhatsApp

100% working.

Step 12 — Public HTTPS URL

Ab Apps Script ko Oracle ke private localhost se connect nahi kar sakte.

Apps Script ko chahiye:

https://something.com

Iske liye main Cloudflare Tunnel recommend karunga.

Aapne Windows par already Cloudflare Tunnel use kiya tha:

trycloudflare.com

Lekin production ke liye quick tunnel ke bajay named Cloudflare Tunnel use karna better hai.

Architecture:

Google Apps Script
       ↓
https://whatsapp.yourdomain.com
       ↓
Cloudflare
       ↓
Oracle Cloud
       ↓
localhost:3000
       ↓
Evolution API

Isse Oracle ka 3000 port directly internet par expose nahi karna padega.

Step 13 — Google Apps Script

Aapki Google Sheet mein maan lo:

A	B	C
Mobile	Message	Status
919XXXXXXXXX	Payment received	
919XXXXXXXXX	Your order is ready	

Apps Script:

function sendWhatsApp(number, message) {


  const url =
    "https://whatsapp.yourdomain.com/message/sendText/Calco-Bot";


  const payload = {
    number: String(number),
    text: message
  };


  const options = {
    method: "post",
    contentType: "application/json",
    headers: {
      "apikey": "YOUR_EVOLUTION_API_KEY"
    },
    payload: JSON.stringify(payload),
    muteHttpExceptions: true
  };


  const response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(url, options);


  Logger.log(response.getResponseCode());
  Logger.log(response.getContentText());


  return response;
}
Step 14 — Sheet se automatically WhatsApp

Aapki Whatsapp sheet ke according, jo aap pehle bana rahe the, hum structure kuch aisa rakh sakte hain:

Mobile	Message	Status
919XXXXXXXXX	Hello Akash	SENT
919XXXXXXXXX	Payment pending	NOT SENT
919XXXXXXXXX	Order ready	SENT

Apps Script:

function sendPendingWhatsApp() {


  const sheet = SpreadsheetApp
    .getActiveSpreadsheet()
    .getSheetByName("Whatsapp");


  const lastRow = sheet.getLastRow();


  if (lastRow < 2) return;


  const data = sheet
    .getRange(2, 1, lastRow - 1, 3)
    .getValues();


  for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {


    const number = data[i][0];
    const message = data[i][1];
    const status = data[i][2];


    if (!number || !message) {
      continue;
    }


    if (status === "SENT") {
      continue;
    }


    try {


      const response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(
        "https://whatsapp.yourdomain.com/message/sendText/Calco-Bot",
        {
          method: "post",


          contentType: "application/json",


          headers: {
            "apikey": "YOUR_EVOLUTION_API_KEY"
          },


          payload: JSON.stringify({
            number: String(number),
            text: String(message)
          }),


          muteHttpExceptions: true
        }
      );


      const code = response.getResponseCode();


      if (code >= 200 && code < 300) {


        sheet
          .getRange(i + 2, 3)
          .setValue("SENT");


      } else {


        sheet
          .getRange(i + 2, 3)
          .setValue("NOT SENT");


      }


    } catch (error) {


      sheet
        .getRange(i + 2, 3)
        .setValue("NOT SENT");


      Logger.log(error);


    }
  }
}
Step 15 — Automatic notification

Phir Apps Script mein:

Triggers → Add Trigger

Function:

sendPendingWhatsApp

Event:

Time-driven

Example:

Every 1 minute

Then system:

Google Sheet
    ↓
Every 1 minute
    ↓
Apps Script
    ↓
Check Status
    ↓
Blank status?
    ↓
Evolution API
    ↓
WhatsApp
    ↓
SENT
Final architecture

Aapka complete production system:

                 ┌──────────────────┐
                 │   Google Sheet   │
                 │                  │
                 │ Mobile           │
                 │ Message          │
                 │ Status           │
                 └────────┬─────────┘
                          │
                          ↓
                 ┌──────────────────┐
                 │ Google Apps      │
                 │ Script           │
                 └────────┬─────────┘
                          │ HTTPS
                          ↓
                 ┌──────────────────┐
                 │    Cloudflare    │
                 │      Tunnel      │
                 └────────┬─────────┘
                          │
                          ↓
              ┌─────────────────────────┐
              │     Oracle Cloud        │
              │                         │
              │ Ubuntu 24.04            │
              │ 2 OCPU + 8 GB RAM       │
              │                         │
              │ ┌─────────────────────┐ │
              │ │ Docker              │ │
              │ │                     │ │
              │ │ Evolution API 2.3.7 │ │
              │ └──────────┬──────────┘ │
              └────────────┼────────────┘
                           │
                           ↓
                     WhatsApp

Oracle Always Free resources lifetime ke liye available hain, although Oracle capacity availability/idle-instance rules apply; current documentation specifically says A1 Always Free allocation is 2 OCPU + 12 GB RAM total.

Hum ise 6 stages mein karenge

Stage 1: Oracle VM create
Stage 2: Docker install
Stage 3: Evolution API 2.3.7 install
Stage 4: WhatsApp Calco-Bot connect + test
Stage 5: Cloudflare HTTPS domain/tunnel
Stage 6: Google Sheet → Apps Script → automatic WhatsApp + SENT/NOT SENT

Abhi sabse pehle Stage 1 karte hain. Aap Oracle Cloud mein Create Instance screen par jao aur VM.Standard.A1.Flex + Ubuntu 24.04 + 2 OCPU + 8 GB + Public IPv4 select karo. Us screen ka screenshot bhej do; main exactly bata dunga kis field mein kya select karna hai.

